  domainId:"home", displayOrder:2, dataStatus:"demo",
  roleInSystem:"Sells fans, air coolers, water heaters, voltage stabilisers, pumps, pressure cookers, mixer-grinders and gas and induction cooktops through electrical dealers and kitchenware shops in every small town, increasingly online. Most products are assembled in India from motors, copper windings, aluminium and steel; brands outsource part of the range to contract makers and spend heavily on dealer schemes.",
  whyItMatters:"These are the first appliances a household buys, so volumes track small-town incomes and new homes. The BEE star-rating rule for ceiling fans (2023) moved buyers to BLDC fans that sell at two to three times the price, and summer heat drives coolers and fans together with ACs. Brands with wide dealer reach hold share against cheap unbranded fans and coolers.",
  valuePoolDescription:"Crompton grew Q2 FY27 revenue 18% with BLDC fans up about 40%, small kitchen appliances (induction cooktops, air fryers) up over 20% and exports up 70%. Havells sells Crompton-style fans plus Lloyd ACs; V-Guard is strongest in the South (stabilisers, water heaters, Sunflame); Bajaj Electricals (Morphy Richards, Nirlep) and Orient (CK Birla group) fight for fans; TTK Prestige and Hawkins lead pressure cookers; Symphony leads air coolers.",
