  whyItMatters:"India is a top supplier of cotton towels and sheets to the US, so US tariffs and UK duties decide these makers' order books. At home, mattresses are moving from unbranded local makers to brands and online sellers, which lets Sheela Foam and Wakefit grow faster than housing.",
  valuePoolDescription:"The US cut its reciprocal tariff on Indian goods from 25% to 18% in Feb 2026 and later moved to a 15% all-country tariff; the India-UK FTA (in force 15 Jul 2026) removed UK duties of about 12% on textiles. Welspun Living grew Q2 FY27 revenue about 16% with home-textile exports up 18% and moved to net cash. Sheela Foam (Sleepwell, Kurlon) and Wakefit (listed 15 Dec 2025) lead branded mattresses; Nilkamal sells plastic furniture and mattresses.",
